  "instructions": [
    "Combine the rice, 3 cups water, and salt in a medium pot. Bring to a boil, cover, and reduce to low. Cook 15 minutes until the water is absorbed, then rest covered.",
    "Whisk the coconut aminos, maple syrup, garlic, and ginger in a small bowl. In a second small bowl, stir the arrowroot into 2 tbsp cold water.",
    "Heat the oil in a 12 inch skillet over medium-high heat. Add the chicken in one layer and cook 5 to 6 minutes, turning once, until browned.",
    "Pour the aminos mixture into the skillet. Simmer 3 minutes, stirring, until the chicken reaches 165 F inside.",
    "Stir the arrowroot mixture again and add it to the skillet. Cook 1 minute until the sauce is glossy and coats the chicken. Move the chicken and sauce to a plate.",
    "Wipe the skillet and add the broccoli and 1/4 cup water. Cover and steam over medium heat 4 to 5 minutes until bright green and tender when pierced with a fork.",
    "Fluff the rice with a fork and divide among four bowls. Top with the chicken, sauce, and broccoli."
